  <data name="Info.Impl.Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>Implications</value></data>
  <data name="Info.Risk.Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>Risks</value></data>
  <data name="Info.Risk.Reversible" xml:space="preserve"><value>Reversible</value></data>
  <data name="Info.Risk.Functional" xml:space="preserve"><value>Functional</value></data>
  <data name="Info.Risk.LowRisk" xml:space="preserve"><value>Low risk</value></data>
  <data name="T_Ads.Impl" xml:space="preserve"><value>You stop seeing ads based on what you do in Windows.</value></data>
  <data name="T_Explorer.Impl" xml:space="preserve"><value>You will see file endings (.exe, .txt) and hidden files, and Explorer opens in This PC.</value></data>
  <data name="T_Taskbar.Impl" xml:space="preserve"><value>Start and icons go back to the left; Widgets and the Task View button disappear.</value></data>
  <data name="T_Search.Impl" xml:space="preserve"><value>Searching in Start only shows your files and apps; web results and Copilot disappear.</value></data>
  <data name="S_Telemetry.Impl" xml:space="preserve"><value>Windows and HP/NVIDIA programs stop running and sending data in the background.</value></data>
  <data name="S_Xbox.Impl" xml:space="preserve"><value>Game Bar (Win+G), game captures and Xbox services disappear.</value></data>
  <data name="S_Maps.Impl" xml:space="preserve"><value>The Maps app and anything using your location (weather, find my device) stops working.</value></data>
  <data name="S_SysMain.Impl" xml:space="preserve"><value>Windows stops guessing which apps you'll open to keep them ready (less idle RAM).</value></data>
  <data name="S_Misc.Impl" xml:space="preserve"><value>4 helpers go off: the one warning about incompatible programs, the shortcut fixer, legacy office networking and the data meter.</value></data>
  <data name="T_Ads.Risk" xml:space="preserve"><value>None. It is reversible and does not affect system stability; it only disables ad personalization and suggestions.</value></data>
  <data name="T_Explorer.Risk" xml:space="preserve"><value>You will see system files: don't delete or move what you don't recognize. The risk is visual and safety-related, not system stability.</value></data>
  <data name="T_Taskbar.Risk" xml:space="preserve"><value>None. This only changes the taskbar layout and appearance; it is reversible.</value></data>
  <data name="T_Search.Risk" xml:space="preserve"><value>If you use Copilot or web suggestions in search, you lose them. The rest of Windows keeps working.</value></data>
  <data name="S_Telemetry.Risk" xml:space="preserve"><value>OMEN/HP and GeForce Experience may lose features; the Feedback Hub app gets no data. It rarely breaks Windows, but it removes diagnostics and OEM telemetry.</value></data>
  <data name="S_Xbox.Risk" xml:space="preserve"><value>If you game or record gameplay with Game Bar, it won't work. It rarely breaks Windows, but it disables the Xbox/Game Bar experience.</value></data>
  <data name="S_Maps.Risk" xml:space="preserve"><value>Maps, location weather and Find my device fail. This is a functional and reversible change, not a system failure.</value></data>
  <data name="S_SysMain.Risk" xml:space="preserve"><value>On spinning hard drives (HDD) programs open slower. On SSD it's barely noticeable. The change is reversible and affects performance, not stability.</value></data>
  <data name="S_Misc.Risk" xml:space="preserve"><value>You won't see warnings installing old programs; some shortcuts may break; the data counter stays empty. Risk is low: it is functional and reversible.</value></data>
</root>
